systerm (0.2.10) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Atlas: FIX a regression — the new header model badge reintroduced the exact
    %-format-over-literal-`alpha='60%'` crash, so the pane (and its right-click
    entry) vanished again after upgrading. Build all such markup by concatenation.
  * Atlas robustness (fixes "doesn't see Ollama / won't analyze"):
    - Detect Ollama even when a GUI's trimmed PATH hides it — also check the common
      absolute paths, and treat a reachable server as proof it's installed.
    - Auto-select a model that's actually downloaded (prefer the configured one,
      then a matching base name, then any qwen/coder model, then the first). The
      hard-coded default meant Ask/Analyze silently did nothing if you'd pulled a
      different model. The header/footer now show the model that will answer.
  * Tests: add tests/test_atlas.py — an AST scan that fails the build on any
    %-format over `alpha='NN%'` markup (no GTK needed), plus model-picker and
    pane-construction tests. Guards against this class of crash recurring.

