systerm (0.2.6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Atlas: FIX the real reason the companion never appeared. The footer built its
    markup with %-formatting over a string containing a literal `alpha='75%'`, so
    Python raised "unsupported format character" every time the pane was
    constructed — silently disabling Atlas and its right-click entry on every
    platform. Build the footer without %-formatting. This is the actual fix for
    the missing "Open Sysible Atlas" menu item.

 -- Sysible <maintainers@sysible.io>  Mon, 10 Aug 2026 14:00:00 +0000

systerm (0.2.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Atlas: the companion pane and its right-click entry ("Open Sysible Atlas")
    no longer disappear when the control FIFO can't be created. The auto-catch
    of failed commands (shell → FIFO) is now initialised separately and
    independently wrapped — if it fails (sandboxed /tmp, no mkfifo), you keep the
    pane, ask box, and Analyze; only hands-free auto-catch is lost. Fixes the
    missing "Open Sysible Atlas" right-click item on some installs.

